sunxi: orangepi-zero: use a conservative boot CPU clock

Set the SPL/U-Boot CPU clock to 480 MHz rather than the H3/H2+ default of
1008 MHz. Follow Armbian's setting to favor boot stability.

Sometimes boot failures with higher boot CPU clocks have been reported on
Orange Pi Zero even when higher clocks work after Linux starts.

The report does not establish the hardware cause or prove the same limit
for every board:
https://forum.armbian.com/topic/15955-issues-building-working-u-boot-for-speeds-above-480mhz-opi-zero/

Armbian reference:
https://github.com/armbian/build/blob/main/patch/u-boot/u-boot-sunxi/board_orangepizero/adjust-small-boards-cpufreq.patch

diff --git a/configs/orangepi_zero_defconfig b/configs/orangepi_zero_defconfig
--- a/configs/orangepi_zero_defconfig
+++ b/configs/orangepi_zero_defconfig
@@ -9,6 +9,7 @@ CONFIG_DRAM_ODT_EN=y
 # CONFIG_VIDEO_DE2 is not set
 CONFIG_SPL_SPI_SUNXI=y
 # CONFIG_SYS_MALLOC_CLEAR_ON_INIT is not set
+CONFIG_SYS_CLK_FREQ=480000000
 CONFIG_CONSOLE_MUX=y
 CONFIG_MTD=y
 CONFIG_SPI_FLASH_MACRONIX=y
